t), or call runtime_notify directly.\n2. consider (redteam, correctness): scripts/merge-gate.py:1163 the bound is checked only between polls. fetch_notes runs `git ls-remote`/`git fetch` with no timeout, so a stalled remote can hold wait-after past `--timeout`. The sleep also does not clip to the time remaining: `--timeout 1` returns after about 10 s at the default interval. The landing itself is not affected; only the wake is late. run-after has the same exposure. Redteam rated this blocking. Gaze downgrades it because no landing is hurt and it needs a hung remote; the dissent is kept here.\n3. consider (correctness): scripts/merge-gate.py:1120 alert_red runs before open_red_ticket while the runner holds the lock, and can delay the ticket by up to 30 s (bounded, exceptions caught).\n4. consider (self): scripts/merge-gate.py:1137 alert_red re-derives the failing names by string match; failing_checks() (merge-gate.py:854) already computes them.\n5. consider (self): scripts/raid_land.py:456 with `idh.afterMerge=off` on a gated base, the printed wake line always ends with exit 2 after 600 s, a ten-minute false wake.\n\nChecked and holding: wait-after exits 0/1/5, an unknown result reads as 1 and the bound gives 2 (tests cover 0/1/2; 5 by code read). The wake line is one shlex-quoted `--cmd` that `cd`s into the primary, run under bash -c by runtime_wake.fire on all three backends. wait-after's 10 s force-fetch of the notes cannot lose the runner's record, because it is pushed by commit id (ticket 1366). An ungated landing prints no line. notify is capped at 30 s and every exception is caught. skills/merge step 9 says to arm the line. Touched tests: selected 17 files (test_after_merge, test_raid_land, test_raid_land_local, test_merge_gate*, ...), fallback: none, result: pass (388 passed).\n\nUnresolved simplify: not planned\n\nduration: 2m55s\ntelemetry: wall=na agents=3 tokens=na cost~=$na\nseat: self \u00b7 runtime=claude-code \u00b7 family=anthropic \u00b7 route=self 